MCP AGENT - DECISION RULES AND EVIDENCE

START: get_manual({}) for topic index; then get_manual({topic:...})
for the relevant operation. 'help CMD' gives CLI syntax. PicoNIX
is not Linux, bash, GCC, GNU as or CPython. Never guess options.

CHOOSE THE TOOL
  get_manual       look up ROM specification; one topic per call
  get_temperature  read board temperature
  execute_command  short, finite, noninteractive CLI; fresh sh -c
  write_file       create/overwrite /tmp/NAME ASCII text
  terminal_read    inspect persistent interactive PTY screen
  terminal_send    type text / key into PTY after checking state
See /man/mcp-workflow for tool limits and /man/terminal-operations
for keyboard, cursor, state and recovery. Six MCP tools total.

ROUTE EACH REQUEST
  1. Identify actual target command, file, device or interface.
  2. Retrieve its manual topic; use help CMD if syntax is unclear.
  3. For observation, prefer bounded read-only execute_command.
     Never cat a streaming /dev node without bounds.
  4. For vi/fd/reversi/other interactive apps, terminal_read FIRST;
     check whether the PTY is at shell prompt or inside an app.
  5. Before any irreversible or hardware-affecting change, obtain
     user approval and inspect file/device/pin ownership.
  6. Execute one action, check its tool result, and independently
     verify observed effects. Report uncertainty explicitly.

DO NOT USE execute_command FOR
  vi, edit, fd, mem interactive view, fbed, watch, reversi, pong,
  bare python REPL, trace follow, or indefinite listeners.
  Short commands may include ps, ip, help, cat of finite files,
  hexdump with count, trace show, pwmctl status, mem -s.
  execute_command has no interactive keyboard; it creates new
  processes, consumes task slots and does not preserve shell cwd.
  See /man/command-reference and /man/shell-syntax.

FAILURE HANDLING
  HTTP timeout / incomplete chunked read does NOT prove failure
  or success of the operation. Do not blindly retry mutations.
  First inspect ps or affected state, then retry only a bounded
  idempotent read if appropriate. terminal_send might have partly
  applied input: inspect terminal_read before further keys.
  If shell was restarted, terminal_send refuses that input; read
  and confirm prompt before issuing a new command.
  If all six user-process slots are occupied, avoid spawning.
  See /man/safety-recovery and /man/debug-checklist.

COMPILATION
  Read /man/languages/c, /man/languages/asm or
  /man/languages/python BEFORE generating code. C cc source <=1024 B.
  C: write /tmp/name.c -> cc -> check -> as -> check -> /tmp/a.out.
  Do not execute a stale /tmp/a.out after an assembly error.
  Use /man/workflows and specific language examples for details.

SECURITY
  MCP exposes remote execution and file writes without auth/TLS.
  Only run on an isolated trusted test LAN; client-side approval
  is required for consequential operations. Never kill mcpd.
  A successful device write does not verify physical behavior.
